## Multi-Tier Caching Architecture

Lament implements an end-to-end caching pipeline spanning three distinct layers: Cloudflare Edge CDN server cache, SvelteKit frontend server proxy, and local browser client cache.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Browser["Browser Client Cache (max-age=3600)"] -->|Cache Miss| CDN["Cloudflare Edge CDN Cache (s-maxage=86400)"]
    CDN -->|Cache Miss| Proxy["SvelteKit Server Proxy (+server.ts)"]
    Proxy -->|API Request| LRU["In-Memory LRU Backend Cache (86400s)"]
    LRU -->|Cache Miss| Storage["Turso LibSQL Database / R2 Storage"]
```

---

## 1. Cloudflare Edge CDN Server Cache (`s-maxage`)

Cloudflare POPs cache static media assets and API payloads at edge locations worldwide to minimize origin server load.

- **Audio Transport Segments (`.ts`)**: Cached immutably at Cloudflare edge POPs (`Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`).
- **WebP Cover Artwork & Artist Photos**: Cached globally with long TTL (`s-maxage=86400`).
- **Lyrics & API Endpoints**: Cached at Cloudflare edge via `s-maxage=86400` directive.

---

## 2. SvelteKit Frontend Server Proxy Layer (`lament`)

The SvelteKit frontend server acts as a proxy shield between client browsers and `lament-api`. Server endpoints (`+server.ts`) inspect upstream responses and inject cache control headers:

```typescript
// Example from src/routes/api/lyrics/[trackId]/+server.ts
setHeaders({
  'cache-control': 'public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=86400'
});
```

- **`s-maxage=86400`**: Directs Cloudflare Edge CDN to cache the response for 24 hours.
- **`max-age=3600`**: Directs the listener's browser to store the response locally for 1 hour.

### HLS Manifest Handling

- **Playlist Index (`playlist.m3u8`)**: SvelteKit proxies playlist index requests and rewrites relative segment URLs through `/api/stream/[id]/[file]` so API keys remain protected server-side.

---

## 3. Browser Client Cache (`max-age` & ETag)

Client browsers (`lament` web player) cache resources locally in HTTP disk and memory cache to ensure instant UI transitions and uninterrupted audio playback.

- **Local Media Caching**: Browsers cache processed WebP images and `.ts` audio segments locally (`max-age=3600` to `max-age=86400`).
- **ETag Validation (`304 Not Modified`)**: API listing endpoints compute MD5/SHA hashes of payload data. When the browser sends `If-None-Match: <etag>`, the server short-circuits execution and returns HTTP 304 with zero body payload.

---

## 4. In-Memory Backend LRU Cache (`CacheService`)

`lament-api` maintains an in-memory LRU (Least Recently Used) cache store:

- **Key Patterns**: `cache:tracks:list`, `cache:artists:<id>`, `lyrics:<track_id>:<variant>`
- **TTL**: High-frequency read queries are cached for 24 hours (86,400 seconds). Search queries are cached for 60 seconds.
- **Instant Invalidation**: Mutation endpoints (`POST /tracks`, `PUT /artists/:id`) invoke `CacheService.delete()` to purge stale entries instantly.

---

## 5. Version-Based Cache Busting (`?v=${updated_at}`)

To completely eliminate stale media playback and eliminate manual Cloudflare R2 cache purges, all media asset URLs are dynamically versioned:

- **Audio & Cover Versioning**: `transformAudioUrl` and `formatImageVariants` append `?v=${updated_at}` (or Unix epoch) to all CDN URLs:
  ```text
  https://cdn.lament.rynds.my.id/hls/trk_123/playlist.m3u8?v=1788609521650
  https://cdn.lament.rynds.my.id/images/covers/trk_123_medium.webp?v=1788609521650
  ```
- **Zero-Purge Instant Invalidation**: When audio or artwork is updated on R2, the updated `updated_at` timestamp immediately bypasses Cloudflare Edge CDN cache and local browser disk cache without requiring manual purges in the Cloudflare dashboard.

---

## 6. Real-Time Catalog Auto-Sync Architecture

Lament keeps listeners' browser clients continuously synchronized with the backend music catalog in real-time:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Mutation["Scraper / Admin inserts Track"] --> DBTrigger["1. Turso Trigger (tracks_catalog_ai)"]
    DBTrigger --> SystemMeta["2. Bumps catalog_version in system_meta"]
    SystemMeta --> SyncPoll["3. SvelteKit Client polls /api/sync/version every 30s"]
    SyncPoll --> VersionMismatch{"New Version Detected?"}
    VersionMismatch -- Yes --> Invalidate["4. Purge client memory & persistentCache + invalidateAll()"]
    Invalidate --> Toast["5. Notify User: 'Katalog musik diperbarui ✨'"]
    VersionMismatch -- No --> Idle["Keep Serving Cached Data"]
```

- **Database-Level Trigger**: Turso automatically increments `catalog_version` in `system_meta` whenever tracks are added, updated, or deleted.
- **Frontend Sync Store (`sync.svelte.ts`)**: Background polling runs every 30 seconds and on tab focus (`visibilitychange`). When a new version is detected, all local client stores and page data caches are refreshed seamlessly.
